DESCRIPTION:Freshman Standardized Testing: Wednesday\, 10/15/14\n\nAll Fres
 hmen\,\nJust a reminder:\nWednesday\, October 15\, you will be taking the E
 ducational Development Series standardized test.\nIt will last approximatel
 y three and a half hours. Please report to your homeroom at 8:00 am.\nYou n
 eed to bring with you two #2 pencils (do NOT bring mechanical pencils).\nCa
 lculators are not allowed for this test.\nThis day is also a dress down day
 .\n\nNO MOBILE PHONES ALLOWED IN EXAM ROOMS.\nOn test day leave your Mobile
  Phones in your Locker!\n\nGood luck on your quarter exams.\nAny questions?
 \nCheck with your Counselor\nThe Counselors\nMrs. See\nMrs. Michalski\nMr. 
 Dougan\nMr. Mouldon\nDr. McKenna\nFr. Heumann\n____________________________
 _____________________________________________\nSOPHOMORES & JUNIORS: PSAT T
 EST ON WEDNESDAY\, 10/15/14\n\nJust a reminder:\nNext week\, Wednesday\, Oc
 tober 15\, you will be taking the PSAT. Please report to your homeroom at 8
 :00 a.m.\nBring with you a calculator (graphing calculator recommended) and
  two #2 pencils (do NOT bring mechanical pencils).\nYou will be finished be
 fore noon.\nMOBILE TELEPHONES ARE NOT PERMITTED IN THE TESTING ROOMS.\nOn t
 he morning of the test\, LEAVE THE PHONES IN YOUR LOCKER.​\nAny questions? 
 Please see your counselor.\nGood luck on your quarter exams.\nThe Counselor
 s:\nMrs. See\nMr. Dougan\nMrs. Michalski\nMr. Mouldon\,\nFr. Heumann\nDr. M
 cKenna
LAST-MODIFIED:20141010T202133Z
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:PSAT and Standardized Testing
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
