BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20181109T010000Z
DTEND:20181109T030000Z
DTSTAMP:20261106T205806Z
UID:0qonql89lqep2o78bvv5i9hkqt@google.com
CREATED:20180925T190543Z
DESCRIPTION:\n\nOn Thursday\, November 8\, from 7:00-9:00 PM\, ACES will be
  hosting\, in the Commons\, a screening of the film Day One\, in conjunctio
 n with the St. Louis International Film Festival.\n\nDay One\n\nLori Miller
 \, 81 min.\, 2018\, U.S.\, in English (with some subtitles)\, documentary f
 eature\n\n“Day One” follows a group of teens from war zones in the Middle E
 ast and Africa as they are resettled in St. Louis and enrolled at Nahed Cha
 pman New American Academy\, a unique school in the St. Louis Public Schools
  system for refugees only. Traumatized on their arrival — having survived w
 ar and years in refugee camps — the kids are guided through an incredible p
 rogram of healing\, PTSD intervention\, education\, and adjustment by the s
 chool’s passionate and talented educators. The featured teens come from Som
 alia\, Afghanistan\, the Congo\, Iraq\, and Syria. These students and their
  families are faced with economic\, language\, psychological\, and cultural
  challenges\, sometimes dangerous living conditions\, and the U.S.’s turbul
 ent anti-immigrant political climate. Filmed over the course of a year\, “D
 ay One” follows the kids as they progress through their layers of grief and
  loss while attending school\, forging new friendships\, and preparing to b
 e mainstreamed into “regular” public high school with the support and mento
 rship of their compassionate teachers and advocates.
LAST-MODIFIED:20180925T190642Z
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:ACES Film Screening
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
