BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20250207T133000Z
DTEND:20250207T211500Z
DTSTAMP:20261106T205806Z
UID:3dj09tvdg471uk61d2jm3bhfmc@google.com
CREATED:20240209T121717Z
DESCRIPTION:<p>The freshman class will participate in its first SLUH retrea
 t this Friday. The retreat is a requirement of the SLUH experience and all 
 freshmen are expected to be there for its entirety. It will be held on our 
 SLUH campus.</p><p> </p><p>Attire for the day is casual. Students should NO
 T bring any homework or electronic devices (they can be left in lockers for
  the day\, if they are needed for transportation purposes). The only thing 
 a student may need is a water bottle\, if he wishes.<br><br></p><ul><li><u>
 7:00 a.m</u>. - Doors open and there is a pancake breakfast to start the da
 y. The earlier students arrive\, the more time they will have to eat with t
 heir class.</li><li><p><u>8:15 a.m.</u> - Everyone should be present by thi
 s time and check in <strong>on the east side of the Si Commons\,</strong> n
 earest the reception desk.</p></li><li><u>3:15 p.m</u>. - The retreat is sc
 heduled to end\, and students can be picked up at this time. There is no di
 nner –  just breakfast\, lunch\, and an afternoon snack. <br><br></li></ul>
 <p>Contact Dr. Kesterson’s office with any attendance issues. Contact Campu
 s Minister Justin Kelley\, SJ (<a href="mailto:jkelley@sluh.org" target="_b
 lank">jkelley@sluh.org</a>) or Chris Stahl (<a href="mailto:cstahl@sluh.org
 " target="_blank">cstahl@sluh.org</a>) with questions about the retreat.</p
 >
LAST-MODIFIED:20250202T234926Z
SEQUENCE:1
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Freshman Retreat
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
